# aie-hash-chain

Python 3.11+ CLI. Hash-Chain mit Ed25519-Signing + O(log n)
Merkle-Inclusion-Proofs für KMU-Audit-Trails (Bell-Labs-Modell:
Sichtbarkeit + Verkettung + Verifizierbarkeit).

Operationalisiert den `consulting-audit-trail`-Skill als ausführbaren
Code: pro Beratungs-/Schulungs-/Compliance-Interaktion drei signierte
Einträge (`geprüft` / `vermittelt` / `offen`) + Merkle-Wurzel + Inclusion-
Proof, den der KMU-Kunde unabhängig verifizieren kann.

## Install (lokal, in venv)

```bash
cd ~/code-aie/aie-hash-chain
python3.12 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -U pip
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

Verify install:

```bash
aie-hash-chain --version
aie-hash-chain --help
```

## 5-Schritt-Demo (copy-paste)

```bash
# 0. activate venv
source .venv/bin/activate

# 1. init chain + Ed25519 keypair
aie-hash-chain init --client "Beispiel KMU GmbH" --output ./demo-client

# 2. append 3 entries (geprüft / vermittelt / offen)
aie-hash-chain append --client-dir ./demo-client \
    --kategorie geprüft --thema "DSGVO Art 13 Newsletter" \
    --quelle "T1: RIS DSG" --datum 2026-05-24

aie-hash-chain append --client-dir ./demo-client \
    --kategorie vermittelt --thema "Empfehlung an DSB" \
    --quelle "Mail an dsb@beispiel-kmu.at" --datum 2026-05-24

aie-hash-chain append --client-dir ./demo-client \
    --kategorie offen --thema "AVV mit Newsletter-Provider" \
    --quelle "GAP — bis 2026-06-15" --datum 2026-05-24

# 3. show current Merkle root
aie-hash-chain merkle-root --client-dir ./demo-client

# 4. emit inclusion proof for one entry (paste an entry id from step 2 output)
ENTRY_ID=$(python3 -c "import json; print(json.load(open('demo-client/chain.json'))['entries'][1]['id'])")
aie-hash-chain inclusion-proof --client-dir ./demo-client \
    --entry-id "$ENTRY_ID" --out proof.json

# 5. verify the proof (this is what the KMU runs)
aie-hash-chain verify --proof proof.json
```

Expected last output:

```
OK signature valid + inclusion-proof reproduces root
```

## Standalone demo script

```bash
python examples/demo_consultation.py
```

Runs the full happy path in a temp directory, prints everything, and
cleans up.

